  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>An institution on the Plage de Pampelonne for more than 50 years, L'Esquinade Plage is literally feet in the sand, facing the sea. Family-friendly, relaxed atmosphere, 200 covers including 150 on the terrace: this is the kind of place where you settle in for the day, between a swim and a meal. Dogs are allowed, which isn't so common on this very busy summer beach.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The restaurant operates in season, from April to October, for lunch and dinner. The beach is private and supervised, with showers, wifi and sunbed/lounger rental on site — handy for combining lazing around and a meal with your dog in the shade. Parking is available on site, but it's best to arrive early in peak summer, as Pampelonne is one of the busiest beaches in the Var.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: follow the Instagram page @esquinade_plage to get a feel for the atmosphere before you come, and consider booking in high season — the 150 terrace spots fill up fast on sunny days.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>You're right in the heart of the Plage de Pampelonne: ideal for combining your lunch break with a long walk by the water. The Saint-Tropez peninsula and its lanes are a few minutes away by car.</p>
